15 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Flowchart showing stages of an in vitro fertilization study: IVF treatment cycles assessed for eligibility, exclusions per criteria, 300 cycles included in final analysis, and 742 embryos included for embryo-level analysis with time-lapse imaging and artificial intelligence data.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Histogram displaying the distribution of AI embryo scores for embryos, with the number of embryos on the y-axis and AI embryo score on the x-axis. Most embryos have scores between 60 and 85, peaking at about 75. A density curve overlays the histogram, indicating a right-skewed distribution.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Bar chart comparing clinical pregnancy rates by score categories: Excellent \(seventy-four percent\), Good \(sixty point two percent\), Moderate \(thirty-nine point one percent\), and Poor \(eighteen point five percent\). Statistical significance is indicated between Excellent, Good, and Moderate groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curve chart illustrating sensitivity versus one minus specificity, with a blue curve indicating a classifier performance and a dashed diagonal line representing random guessing; area under the curve \(AUC\) is labeled as zero point eight nine.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Horizontal bar chart illustrating the relative feature importance of variables in a model. AI Embryo Score ranks highest at 1.00, followed by Blastocyst Quality at 0.85, Maternal Age at 0.72, AMH Level at 0.58, and Fertilization Rate at 0.44.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
